 2: N_tot = 120, random B = 100, 10 protocols; P(report > truth) / coverage with intervals, width and deployed-accuracy cost in accuracy points; real and synthetic columns. It carries the anti-conservative score only (Fig 4 has the pair). It sets its own \\\\footnotesize and \\\\tabcolsep 2pt and is 5.49 in wide, 2.0 in high: place it at full text width. Šidák and evaluated-set Bonferroni are not drawn (Šidák = Bonferroni within .001).\n3. Merging: Fig 4 already fills the 5.5 × 2.3 in with three panels and 11 rows, so a Fig 5 panel would not fit without enlarging the figure to about 4 in high, which saves only ~0.5 in against two floats. If you need the space, a cheaper cut is Fig 5 at N_tot = 120 only (one panel, 2.7 in wide; the 240 panel adds nothing new: same pattern); tell me and I redraw it, otherwise leave both as they are.\" 2>&1 | tail -1; forge issue close 3 2>&1 | tail -1"]], "output": "```console\nhttp://172.17.0.1:32789/world/figtab-repo/issues/3#issuecomment-63\nClosed #3\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "20a2f01e-1149-54fb-8a95-fc900ab28e29", "at": 1795696208.1299295, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 44288, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "figtab-repo", "actor": "figtab-repo", "execution_id": "da3f91e16a45a6897c82d58e1bc65c91", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "996de13b-3071-57ae-8866-933ac5c51d0e", "at": 1795696208.1379018, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 44289, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "figtab-repo", "actor": "figtab-repo", "execution_id": "da3f91e16a45a6897c82d58e1bc65c91", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "cb9dabb4-b9a4-54bf-b646-6dc6c413c390", "at": 1795696208.141559, "cl